A||||6||jeffozz||Swap Meet Info Forwarded (from Ed Parks)||||1||
Z||000000||jeffozz||04-14-2001||12:45 AM||||List Friends, looking forward to seeing/meeting y'all on the 27-29th for the 3rd Annual (maybe last) All Fiero Flea Market and Swap Meet.<BR>This is NOT the Ed Parks or Fiero Factory event, we merely have the room to host it. Many Fiero Folks help in putting it together. From cleaning, mowing, moving cars out of the way, to taking care of the T-shirts, kitchen, and raffle "stuff".<BR>It does cost us considerable out of pocket "up front" expenses for <BR>food, drinks, tents, and porta-potties, and these expenses are covered by raffles.<BR>This year, there will be a powered coated, polished and cleared coated,<BR>engraved pleneum and set of valve covers for $10 per ticket.<BR>Also, $300 off of Mr Mikes leather covers for $10 per ticket.<BR>A set of The Fiero Shops hood scoops for $5 per ticket and a 1/2 pot sale that is $1 for 4 tickets or an arm length of <BR>tickets for $5.<BR>There have also been a number of smaller "door prize" types of donations.<BR>These will be in the form of grab bags for either $2 or $5 each. <BR>There won't be too many, so first come will be first served.<BR>There should be many Fiero parts brought by folks, and a number of parts/driver cars for sale.<BR>There will be hotdogs, chili dogs, nacho's w/salsa and cheese, chips, and<BR>cold drinks for sale on the premises.<BR>Hope everyone can come and have a good time.<P>Do we need to be present to win? Some of us have to scram out Saturday afternoon/evening to make it home for work on Monday.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Eric, to keep down a lot of paper work (and perhaps hard feelings), you<BR>would have to be present to win. <P>Swap Meet times are 8:30-5:30. Gates will be locked and Sheriffs patrols<BR>increased during the night so parts displays won't have to be reloaded.<P>To answer some other questions that we did not address, the raffle<BR>drawings will be at 2 pm on Sat (will be quick so folks can get back to<BR>swapping). If anyone can't be there at that time, please don't buy<BR>tickets. After that time, if needed/wanted parts have not been found at<BR>the Swap Meet, only then will The Fiero Factory be "open for business" to<BR>sell ours. An example of why: last year an early attendee on Thurs wanted<BR>an outer door panel (we sell them for $70), which we refused to sell.<BR>During the Swap meet he bought an entire door w/panel for $5!! <P>David Hunter will again have tee shirts for this event ($15) and a few<BR>left from the previous events  ($5) and since he has funded them, just<BR>hopes to get his $$ back. Please support him. David has done this each<BR>year, and for that we thank him very much. <P>Many folks must leave late Sat since they have come from far away (last<BR>year from 26 states), and some don't want to load up parts and take them<BR>back home. So, Sunday is really a bargain day for those that remain.<BR>Anything left behind is FREE for just picking them up (saves the staff<BR>some extra work on Monday!!). <P>Also forgot to ask, that since we are not on Pennocks Forum, the TechNet,<BR>or the Fiero.org lists, would anyone mind forwarding this?<P>Thanks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bill Osmer||04-14-2001||10:18 PM||||This post doesn't give any idea where the flea market is being held... Can someone fill in the blanks??<P>Bill||||reg||5
Z||000002||Raydar||04-14-2001||10:31 PM||||The Flea Market is being held at The Fiero Factory, in Toney Alabama. It's on Hwy 53, about 20 miles north of Huntsville Alabama. If you come up 53, it's on the right, just after you cross the bridge.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||04-19-2001||08:59 AM||||FYI here is the link to Ed's site.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#top" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#top</A> <P>Hope to see you there.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||04-19-2001||03:04 PM||||Just made my reservations at LaQuinta East on University Drive (Hwy 72).<BR>$53.99/nite, if you have a SAMS Club card.<BR>256-533-0756. (It's on the same side of the street as, and within stumbling distance of, Ed and Rosy's favorite Mexican restaurant.)<P>Many folks are also staying at the Comfort Inn. 256-533-3291,<BR>Or Holiday Inn Express. 256-721-1000.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||87ECO5||04-19-2001||07:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jeffozz:<BR><B>This is NOT the Ed Parks or Fiero Factory event, we merely have the room to host it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm confused.  This is not the Fiero Factory event but it's being held at the Fiero Factory on the same weekend as Ed's swap meet?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000006||mrfiero||04-19-2001||07:52 PM||||What Ed means is that it isn't an Ed Parks or Fiero Factory event, but rather OUR event.  Ed closes his shop during most of the weekend so everyone who comes down to sell stuff gets a chance to without competing with the Fiero Factory and it's huge inventory.<P>He charges no admission fee or vendors fees for this event.....meaning that they are hosting the event, but not profiting from it.  There are inherent costs associated with hosting a swap meet, which is where the raffles come in.......they money raised through the raffles helps offset the costs of the port-a-potty's, etc.<P>This is an opportunity for regular Joe's or small vendors (like myself) to reach a few hundred Fiero people at once to buy, sell, trade, whatever Fiero stuff we want. <BR> <BR>There will be many great deals to be had, so everyone who can attend should attend.  Bring a truck, not your Fiero, so you can haul away all of your goodies......I will have a TON of stuff at giveaway prices, so I hope you all come!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
